+Lane: `code-factory-pm`. Work done in a clean clone of `origin/main` at `80fca8b` (the shared
+checkout was left untouched: four sibling lanes were `running` at tick start). Paths here are
+repo-relative; no host paths or worktree names are recorded.
+
+## What the PRD/plan claimed, and what the tree actually is
+
+Measured at `80fca8b`:
+
+| Claim | Source | Measured | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 15 selftest sections | `docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md` snapshot | 28 sections (`grep -cE '^say "[0-9]+\.' tests/selftest.sh`) | stale |
+| 34 `PASS` rows | same | 70 `PASS` rows, suite counter `fails=0`, rc 0 | stale |
+| 68 task rows / 74 events | same | 85 rows / 115 events at `80fca8b` | stale (true only at its pinned tip) |
+| three legs blocked by `CF-075`, `CF-077`, `CF-080` | `docs/PRD-code-factory.md` milestone block | `CF-075` **complete** (`77caa02`, selftest §16), `CF-077` **complete** (`1232f7a`, §17/§18), `CF-080` pending | two of three false |
+| "No arm covers layers 00, 10, 20, 30 or 40 individually" (`CF-102`) | PRD requirement table | layer 00 ← §3 and §20, layer 20 ← §14, layer 40 ← §4/§4b, layer 30 ← §15 pair; **layer 10 has no arm** | understated coverage |
+
+The plan's numbers reproduce at the tip it pinned (`400a5ab`), so they were honest when written and
+became stale when six selftest commits landed (§16–§28). The PRD milestone block was the real defect:
+it still cited two closed rows as live blockers, which makes a reader think the create path is broken
+when the staged-set gap has been closed and proven in the gate.
+
+The `docs/BOARD.md` "Current measured state" block is stale in the same way (61 rows / 66 events /
+17 warnings claimed; 85 / 115 / 28 measured). That is already row `CF-081`, which requires a
+*committed check* plus a red arm, so this tick did not restate it.
+
